Z||000011||88formula||07-18-2000||05:25 PM||||GT Bastard, I almost did the 3.2 rebuild as I suspect you are doing now. I have chosen to put in a 3.4 Camaro engine with 51,000 miles because it is actually cheaper and more powerful than the 3.2 with the Silvolite 8.8 compression pistons. The 3.4 engine has a stock 9.0 compression ratio. The biggest hurdle is drilling the starter holes. If you want to do this swap I can help you with the starter holes, just e-mail me.<P>The heads that came with the 93 3.4 Camaro engine are the same as the fiero heads. I don’t know about the 3.1.<BR>||||reg||1
